specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:8:Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:12:- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:13:- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:14:- A rejected type error identifies the property path and expected type without including the invalid value ([validated by rejects a wrong-typed property reports its field path without the offending value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L55)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:15:- A rejected nested type error identifies the full instance path and expected type ([validated by: reports a nested wrong-typed property by its full instance path](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L117)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:16:- A rejected type error recovers the property path from validator metadata when an instance path is unavailable ([validated by: recovers a property path when the validator omits instancePath](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L141)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:17:- Public rejection messages use `must` wording for type failures, even when the validator supplies legacy `should` wording ([validated by: normalizes validator type wording to the public must form](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L151)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:18:- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input and undeclared properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L5)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:23:- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:24:- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles a static schema once across repeated executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L30)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:25:- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates each function-valued definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L55)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:29:- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
